\title{crate: Canonical Schemas for Changing Data and Provenance Receipts}
\description{
\if{html}{\figure{logo.png}{options: style='float: right' alt='logo' width='120'}}

Declares a canonical shape for each kind of file or table it registers, reads a registered file to that shape whichever known layout arrives, and holds data read some other way to the same shape, so a change in a registered file's columns or layout is fixed once in crate rather than in every reader downstream. Also holds the provenance receipt contract: a JSON Schema, RFC 8785 canonical JSON, a table fingerprint and test vectors, with R functions that write receipts and compare two builds as identical, equivalent within a declared tolerance, or different. Under active development.
